tip: | Compare it with the dog. | Same plan: head up, chest, haunch, tail. Pointed ears, a short face and an upright tail do the rest.
tip: 1 | Change the ends. | Most of an animal is one body. Swap the head and tail and a dog turns into a cat, so start from those.
tip: 3 | Same ramp plan. | Light on the head and chest, dark on the low back, like the dog on a redder ramp. Pale eyes stand out against it, so they are the one detail it needs.
tip: | The other facing. | The tail is what a mirror shows up: it swaps sides with the head, so the whole cat looks the other way. Nothing needed redrawing.
